blueprint v1
size: 5 5 4
axes: x west->east, z north->south, y up; layer y0 = the feet level
// The Demo-3 design's example (build.out.md §3.2) with the critique's findings
// 1 and 4 applied: the torch stands on the floor at (2, 0, 1) instead of on the
// north wall at head height, because a wall torch arrives as
// minecraft:wall_torch and the place receipt would never settle. Counts, pinned
// by the crate's tests: 71 cobblestone walls + 2 entry cells = 73 placements,
// plus 1 torch = 74 cells. The unused `_` entry is deliberate: it exercises the
// unused-palette warning.
palette:
  W: cobblestone
  T: torch
  .: air
  e: cobblestone entry
  _: keep
layer y0:
WWWWW
W.T.W
W...W
W...W
WWeWW
layer y1:
WWWWW
W...W
W...W
W...W
WWeWW
layer y2:
WWWWW
W...W
W...W
W...W
WWWWW
layer y3:
WWWWW
WWWWW
WWWWW
WWWWW
WWWWW
